{%- comment -%}
  Renders the TikTok mark used in the footer's social row.

  Drawn to the Phase 2 contract - 24x24 canvas, stroke 1.5, currentColor, round
  caps and joins - so the mark follows --accent-current, a hover and either
  surface. The prototype's raster PNGs could not: colour is baked into their
  pixels (Phase 1 classifies both as "replace with SVG snippet").

  NOT THE OFFICIAL BRAND ASSET. PHASE-3-ASSET-SYSTEM.md records that platform
  marks should come from each platform's own brand kit as SVG and be used
  unmodified. This is a stroke-weight approximation drawn to match the rest of
  the icon set, which is what the approved footer design shows. Swap it for the
  official asset before launch if the brand guidelines are to be followed to the
  letter.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} optional extra class names

  Usage:
  {% render 'icon-tiktok' %}

  Decorative: the link that wraps it carries the accessible name, so the mark is
  aria-hidden.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="icon icon--tiktok {{ class }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9.5 11.75a4.25 4.25 0 1 0 4.25 4.25V3.75a5.25 5.25 0 0 0 5.25 5.25"/></svg>
